# Windy Git CI (dind + the 6 act_runners) as its OWN top-level slice, so it gives way to
# everything else on Veron 1 under contention (Boss GO 2026-10-27, for the sign-up journeys).
#
# Why top-level, not a weight on the dind scope: CPU weights only compete between siblings.
# dind's scope sat in system.slice and the journeys are user units in user.slice, so a weight
# on one never met the other; what decided CI vs. everyone was system.slice 100 : user.slice 100.
# Weight 50 since 2026-10-28 (Boss GO 20:04Z runtime, 10-29 16:00Z persistent): at 20, a busy
# spike left CI about 4 cores for 2-3 jobs and load-timeout flakes followed. As a sibling of
# system/user/windy (100 each), CI's floor is now 50/150 (~33%, ~8 cores) when only the lanes
# compete, still 2:1 behind user.slice, where the journey VMs (1000) live, and it runs at full
# speed (up to dind's own cpus: 12 cap) when idle. Measured 10-28 20:02Z..10-29 16:00Z: CI cpu
# some avg10 p95 2.8% (5.4% in busy minutes), user.slice some p95 22%, unchanged from before.
# CI gets slower under load; it never stops.
#
# No IOWeight: the main disk (nvme0n1) runs the "none" scheduler, where io weights do nothing.
#
# Install: cp deploy/runner/windygitci.slice /etc/systemd/system/ && systemctl daemon-reload
# The containers join it through `cgroup_parent: windygitci.slice` in docker-compose.yml,
# applied by deploy/runner/recreate-idle.sh (never kills a running job).
# Rollback: remove cgroup_parent from docker-compose.yml, run recreate-idle.sh again, then
#   rm /etc/systemd/system/windygitci.slice && systemctl daemon-reload
[Unit]
Description=Windy Git CI (dind + runners): yields CPU to everything else under contention
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
CPUWeight=50
